  "description": "The dialect seam of Fuaran.Modelling — the public extension point behind which all model vocabulary lives. Six obligations as one typed interface (spec-tree types, validators, a projector rendering the tree to canonical payload bytes, a parse-back importer with a residue report, a default gate vocabulary on the generic (name, threshold, direction) triple, and a pack schema), an executable conformance corpus with stable failure codes, a versioned seam whose skew is a typed refusal, and a trivial reference dialect that binds the contract. The default spec-hash minting rule is the registered canonical-json-sha256-v1, taken from the execution tier rather than reimplemented here, so one identifier never names two rules. FSharp.Core plus the Fuaran.Core substrate; no estimator, no numerical method.",
